{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And from the wilderness to Mattanah, and from Mattanah to Nahaliel, and from Nahaliel to Bamoth, and from Bamoth to the valley.</b> R. Yehudah says: from the wilderness — Israel merited that the Torah was given to them through Moses, as it is said (Exodus 31:18): ״ויתן אל משה״; and from Mattanah — they inherited idolatry, as they said: ״אלה אלהיך ישראל״; and from Nahaliel to Bamoth — and once they inherited idolatry, death came, as it is said (Numbers 14:35): ״במדבר הזה יתמו ושם ימותו״; and from Bamoth to the valley — an allusion to that righteous one who would be buried in the valley, who would not enter the land — this is what Jeremiah says (Jeremiah 2:23): ״ראי דרכך בגיא״. Thus they expounded in the Midrash Tehillim (Psalms 5:1): למנצח אל הנחילות." "<b>And in the Tanhuma:</b> וממדבר מתנה — if a person makes himself ownerless (hefker) in the labor of Torah, like the wilderness which is ownerless to all, it is given to him as a gift, as it is said: וממדבר מתנה. And once it is given to him as a gift, he inherits El, as it is said: וממתנה נחליאל. And once he inherits El, he rises to greatness; and if he becomes haughty, the Holy One, blessed be He, humbles him, as it is said: ומבמות הגיא. And if he repents, the Holy One, blessed be He, raises him up, as it is said (Isaiah 40:4): ״כל גיא ינשא״." "<b>And by way of</b> the Kabbalah: אז ישיר ישראל את השירה הזאת — the שירה, like the תפלה, draws the intention in one's thought from above downward; so too the individual or the community who recite שירה draw blessing from above downward." "<b>And know</b> that שיר״ה in gematria is תפל״ה, and it is written (Psalms 42:9): ״יומם יצוה ה׳ חסדו ובלילה שירה עמי״ — שירה is written; ״תפלה לאל חיי״. And it says את השירה הזאת — you already know what זאת is, for זאת is emanated from זאת, and this is what it says: ״תפלה לאל חיי״ — אומרה לאל סלעי, and this is the secret of the verse (Lamentations 2:19): ״קומי רני בלילה״ — עם המלכות ידבר הזאת לראש אשמורות, for it did not say בראש. And the masters of the peshat who did not know this were forced to say that the למ״ד is in place of a בי״ת. עלי באר ענו לה — one must begin from below upward in order to elevate the tenth attribute to the place of its source, and afterward draw the blessings from there, drawing and continuing from above downward; and this is what it says: עלי באר ענו לה — that is, it is upon us to praise this attribute and to say to it: עלי באר. And it called this attribute a באר (well) because it receives power from all of them and is emanated from them, for a well is a vessel that receives waters, and therefore it always likens it in the Sefer ha-Bahir to a throne and a vessel, and it says there: למלך שהיה לו כסא, למלך שהיה לו כלי נאה ומבושם. And from this it mentioned ומשם בארה with the addition of the ה״א, and it is the final ה״א of the Name. And the meaning of עלי באר: ascend to the place from which you were hewn. חפרוה שרים — Wisdom and Understanding. נדיבי העם — Greatness, Might, and Beauty; they are Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob, who are called thus, as it is said (Psalms 47:10): ״נדיבי עמים נאספו״. במחוקק — this is צדיק, the Foundation of the World. במשענותם — Netzaḥ and Hod. Thus the entire structure is alluded to in the language of this שירה, just as it is alluded to in the Song of the Sea. וממתנה נחליאל — they said in the Sefer ha-Bahir: do not read נחליאל but rather נחלי אל; these are the seven that are called נחל. And ממתנה is the brain, that is, Wisdom, from which all the seven are emanated; and these channels (נחלים) go to the Sea by way of Yesod, and they need to ascend and receive and draw flow from the supernal source, which is called במות, and likewise in the Targum: רמתא. And this is what the Prophet, peace be upon him, mentioned (Habakkuk 3:10): ״רום ידיהו נשא״, and it is the segolta that comes after the zarka, for the zarka alludes to the tenth one which ascends after the segolta that is above all, and therefore the segolta is three points and is above the word, and this is the secret of (Psalms 135:4–5): ״כי יעקב בחר לו יה ישראל לסגולתו״ — for the יו״דד with its point and the ה״א is the segolta. ומבמות הגיא — for after they ascend to draw, they empty the valley — that is אשר בשדה מואב: do not read מואב but rather מאב — that about which it is said (Genesis 26:5): ״עקב אשר שמע אברהם בקולי״, and the intention is upon the attribute of חסד which is the first of the attributes, and therefore it says: ראש הפסגה. And this is the meaning of the verse (Psalms 133:2): ״כשמן הטוב על הראש״ — it likened the flow to good oil and said that it is poured upon the head, which is the במות and the segolta, and that flow descends first upon the beard — זקן אהרן — descending according to its attributes exactly. ונשקפה על פני הישימון — על פני השמים, and it is rendered שמיא; and the meaning is that when the attributes are blessed by receiving the flow of blessing from above, the world of separate beings is blessed, and the heavens and all their hosts."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:34:59.685022683Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}